description:
When releaseTunnel() fails (ngrok disconnect throws), the TunnelInfo entry is NOT removed from activeTunnels (stopTunnel re-throws on error without deleting). On the next call for the same localhost port, findTunnelByPort() returns the stale entry and the handler uses a dead tunnel URL as the public URL.

Relevant code in stopTunnel():
  try {
    await ngrok.disconnect(tunnelInfo.tunnelUrl);
    this.activeTunnels.delete(tunnelId);  ← only runs on success
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error(...);
    throw error;  ← stale entry remains
  }

Fix: delete from activeTunnels unconditionally before disconnect, not after:
  this.activeTunnels.delete(tunnelId);     ← remove first
  if (tunnelInfo.autoShutoffTimer) clearTimeout(tunnelInfo.autoShutoffTimer);
  await ngrok.disconnect(tunnelInfo.tunnelUrl).catch(err => logger.warn(...));  ← best-effort

If disconnect fails we still want the entry gone — a dead tunnel in the map is worse than a leaked ngrok connection (ngrok times those out anyway).

credentialWarning fires "signed in with an environment default credential" on a login that was REFUSED and never submitted anything (isEnvironmentDefault ignores login.submitted)

OBSERVED: mcp__debugg-ai-published__check_app_in_browser execution 2d4970a6-c443-4b1b-ad84-e9aa03f65450 (url=https://crochets.site/pricing, auth={precondition:'login', entryUrl:'https://auth.startsimpli.com/signin?...', deepUrl:'https://crochets.site/pricing', username, password}, top-level username/password also set, useEnvironmentCredentials:false). The run's logins evidence was [{reason:'no_login_form_detected', source:'explicit'}, {reason:'offscope_host', source:'env_default'} x2] -- i.e. every attempt was a deliberate SKIP (host out of scope; see sibling bead sentinal-81g87 in platform/sentinal for why), nothing was ever typed or submitted. The response nonetheless carried:

  credentialWarning: { requested: '<the named account>', used: [...], message: "This run signed in with an environment default credential even though '<account>' was specified. Treat a login failure here as a credential-resolution problem, not an application failure." }

That message is false on its face for this run -- no credential was ever entered anywhere, the run never signed in as anyone. It steers a caller straight past the actual bug (the offscope refusal) toward a nonexistent credential-substitution problem.

ROOT CAUSE (confirmed on origin/main):

services/verdictAdapter.ts:90-91:
  export function isEnvironmentDefault(login: LoginRecord): boolean {
    return !!login.source && !CALLER_SPECIFIED_SOURCES.has(login.source);
  }
This checks ONLY login.source (true whenever source isn't 'task'/'explicit'/'credential_id', which includes 'env_default'/'env'). It never looks at login.submitted or login.authenticated.

handlers/testPageChangesHandler.ts:863-878:
  const requestedIdentity = input.username ?? input.auth?.username ?? input.loginCredentials?.[0]?.username;
  const substituted = (verdict.logins ?? []).filter(isEnvironmentDefault);
  if (requestedIdentity && substituted.length > 0) {
    responsePayload.credentialWarning = { ... "This run signed in with an environment default credential..." ... }
  }
This fires whenever ANY logins entry has a non-caller source, including a {submitted:false, reason:'offscope_host', source:'env_default'} SKIP record that never typed a single character. The message text ("signed in with") is specifically false for exactly this case.

Not a duplicate of debugg_ai_mcp-qqvr (the P0 bead that originally motivated adding logins/loginError/credentialWarning to the response) -- qqvr is about a credential actually being WRONGLY SUBSTITUTED AND USED at a login form; this bug is the warning firing on a login that was never attempted at all.

SUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION (not prescriptive): gate isEnvironmentDefault (or its caller) on login.submitted being true (or exclude records whose `reason` marks a deliberate skip, e.g. offscope_host/no_login_form_detected), so the warning only fires when an environment-default credential was actually typed/submitted somewhere.

Type: bug. Priority: P2 -- misleading diagnostic text, doesn't block the run, but actively misdirects debugging of the offscope_host issue (sentinal-81g87) it co-occurs with.
